  <data name="AboutTitle.Text"><value>About – Best Practices &amp; Sources</value></data>
  <data name="AboutIntro.Text"><value>This app reads the local hardening state (registry, secedit, Defender, BitLocker, firewall and audit APIs) and compares it against recognized best practices – passed / failed / manual review, each with a severity.</value></data>
  <data name="AboutSourcesHeader.Text"><value>Best practices used</value></data>
  <data name="AboutCisBody.Text"><value>Based on CIS Microsoft Windows 11 Benchmark v5.0.0. Level 1: essential hardening without loss of functionality (curated subset of 91 of the ~390 L1 recommendations). Level 2: defense-in-depth for high-security environments. Stand-alone / Enterprise profiles via the target selector. Only technical target values are checked - no CIS texts adopted. (cisecurity.org/cis-benchmarks)</value></data>
  <data name="AboutMsBody.Text"><value>Machine-imported from the Security Compliance Toolkit (GPO registry, SecEdit, Advanced Audit, firewall, services; as of build 26200.6584). Checks GPO enforcement – deviations are expected on devices without an applied baseline. Deltas possible on 26H2. (aka.ms/SCT)</value></data>
  <data name="AboutStigBody.Text"><value>Cross-reference for target values and severity classification. (cyber.mil/STIGs)</value></data>
  <data name="AboutMethodHeader.Text"><value>Methodology</value></data>
  <data name="AboutMethodBody.Text"><value>Severities: Critical (credential/LSA/encryption protection), High (firewall, Defender, accounts, user rights), Medium (audit, hardening), Low/Info (convenience, telemetry). Status: passed, failed, manual review (admin rights or hardware-dependent), error. Checks run limited without admin rights (net-accounts fallback, otherwise manual flag).</value></data>
  <data name="AboutRulesNote.Text"><value>Rule texts are available in English and German; technical references (policy paths, registry keys, auditpol commands) stay in their source language.</value></data>
